  <datafield tag="590" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Cover of Getty copy is by Rodchenko.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="590" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Getty copy has embossed owner's mark at lower right-hand corner of last leaf, ca. 15 mm. in width. It consists of the Russian Imperial eagle over ROVARD in Cyrillic letters.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="590" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Housed with Getty copy is a monitoring template.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Hand-produced catalog of the exhibition, to which each of the five artists contributed five works. The catalog includes one work by each artist. Additions and corrections in ink throughout.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">First leaf is title in carbon typescript, over which "5 x 5 = 25" has been written in red, green and purple gouache. Leaves [2]-[6] are hectographed and list each artist's works; those for Stepanova, Popova and Exter include brief statements on art. Leaf [7]: abstract composition by Exter in gouache, signed A.Ė. at lower right. Leaf [8]: two crossed lines in red and blue pencil on graph paper by Rodchenko, signed r. at lower left. Leaf [9]: abstract composition by Popova in colored pencils, signed L.P. in red at lower left. Leaf [10]: abstract composition in brown ink by Vesnin, signed A.V. in pencil at lower right. Leaf [11]: blank. Leaf [12]: mounted linocut(?) by Stepanova, signed Varsh in ink below at right.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Covers of the catalog are by Rodchenko or Stepanova.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Stab sewn with red string.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="583" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
